                <!-- Table API -->
                <section class="content-section" id="table-api">
                    <h2>Table API</h2>
                    <p>
                        There is no dedicated "IRM API" — you interact with IRM data using the standard 
                        ServiceNow <strong>Table API</strong>. This means all CRUD operations follow the same 
                        patterns you'd use for any ServiceNow table.
                    </p>

                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">
                            <span class="code-lang">REST — GET All High Risks</span>
                            <button class="code-copy">Copy</button>
                        </div>
                        <div class="code-body">
<pre><code>GET /api/now/table/sn_risk_risk
    ?sysparm_query=residual_risk=high
    &sysparm_fields=sys_id,name,state,profile.name,residual_risk
    &sysparm_display_value=true
    &sysparm_limit=50

Headers:
  Accept: application/json
  Authorization: Basic {credentials}</code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">
                            <span class="code-lang">REST — Create a New Risk</span>
                            <button class="code-copy">Copy</button>
                        </div>
                        <div class="code-body">
<pre><code>POST /api/now/table/sn_risk_risk

Headers:
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json

Body:
{
    "name": "Data breach risk for Customer Portal",
    "description": "Risk of unauthorized access to customer PII",
    "profile": "{entity_sys_id}",
    "risk_owner": "{user_sys_id}",
    "state": "draft"
}</code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">
                            <span class="code-lang">REST — Query Controls by Entity</span>
                            <button class="code-copy">Copy</button>
                        </div>
                        <div class="code-body">
<pre><code>GET /api/now/table/sn_compliance_control
    ?sysparm_query=profile={entity_sys_id}
    &sysparm_fields=sys_id,name,state,policy_statement.name
    &sysparm_display_value=true</code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- GlideRecord -->
                <section class="content-section" id="gliderecord">
                    <h2>GlideRecord Patterns</h2>
                    <p>
                        For server-side scripting (Business Rules, Script Includes, Scheduled Jobs), 
                        <strong>GlideRecord</strong> is the primary mechanism for querying and manipulating IRM data.
                    </p>

                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">
                            <span class="code-lang">GlideRecord — Find All Entities of a Specific Type</span>
                            <button class="code-copy">Copy</button>
                        </div>
                        <div class="code-body">
<pre><code>// Find all entities of type "Critical Windows Servers"
var gr = new GlideRecord('sn_grc_profile');
gr.addQuery('profile_type.name', 'Critical Windows Servers');
gr.addActiveQuery();
gr.query();

while (gr.next()) {
    gs.info('Entity: ' + gr.name + 
            ' | CI: ' + gr.applies_to.getDisplayValue() +
            ' | Class: ' + gr.profile_class.getDisplayValue());
}</code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">
                            <span class="code-lang">GlideRecord — Get Failed Controls for an Entity</span>
                            <button class="code-copy">Copy</button>
                        </div>
                        <div class="code-body">
<pre><code>// Find all controls in "Monitor" state that have failed
// indicators for a specific entity
var entitySysId = '...'; // your entity sys_id

var gr = new GlideRecord('sn_compliance_control');
gr.addQuery('profile', entitySysId);
gr.addQuery('state', 'monitor');
gr.query();

while (gr.next()) {
    // Check if this control has any failed indicators
    var ind = new GlideRecord('sn_grc_indicator');
    ind.addQuery('item', gr.sys_id);
    ind.addQuery('last_result', 'fail');
    ind.query();
    
    if (ind.hasNext()) {
        gs.info('FAILED CONTROL: ' + gr.name +
                ' | Owner: ' + gr.owned_by.getDisplayValue());
    }
}</code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">
                            <span class="code-lang">GlideRecord — Create an Issue from Script</span>
                            <button class="code-copy">Copy</button>
                        </div>
                        <div class="code-body">
<pre><code>// Programmatically create a GRC Issue
var issue = new GlideRecord('sn_grc_issue');
issue.initialize();
issue.name = 'Access control failure on ' + entityName;
issue.description = 'Automated detection: MFA not enforced';
issue.profile = entitySysId;  // Link to entity
issue.item = controlSysId;    // Link to control
issue.priority = '2';         // High
issue.assigned_to = ownerSysId;
issue.insert();

gs.info('Created issue: ' + issue.number);</code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- Scripted Indicators -->
                <section class="content-section" id="scripted-indicators">
                    <h2>Scripted Indicators</h2>
                    <p>
                        Scripted indicators are one of the most common development tasks in IRM. They use 
                        server-side JavaScript to query data across the platform and determine if a control 
                        is passing or failing.
                    </p>

                    <h3>Indicator Script Structure</h3>
                    <p>
                        Every scripted indicator receives two objects: <code>control</code> (the control record 
                        being evaluated) and <code>indicator</code> (the indicator configuration). The script 
                        must return one of three values:
                    </p>

                    <div class="data-table-wrapper">
                        <table class="data-table">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Return Value</th>
                                    <th>Meaning</th>
                                    <th>When to Use</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>'pass'</code></td>
                                    <td>Control is effective</td>
                                    <td>The verified condition is met</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>'fail'</code></td>
                                    <td>Control is not effective</td>
                                    <td>The verified condition is NOT met</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>'not_applicable'</code></td>
                                    <td>Control doesn't apply</td>
                                    <td>Entity doesn't have the prerequisites for this check</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>

                    <div class="tabs-container">
                        <div class="tabs-header">
                            <button class="tab-btn active" data-tab="tab-ind-patch">Patch Compliance</button>
                            <button class="tab-btn" data-tab="tab-ind-incident">Incident SLA</button>
                            <button class="tab-btn" data-tab="tab-ind-change">Change Approval</button>
                        </div>

                        <div class="tab-panel active" id="tab-ind-patch">
                            <div class="code-block">
                                <div class="code-header">
                                    <span class="code-lang">Scripted Indicator — Patch Compliance Check</span>
                                    <button class="code-copy">Copy</button>
                                </div>
                                <div class="code-body">
<pre><code>// Check: Are all critical patches applied within 30 days?
(function(control, indicator) {
    var ci = control.profile.applies_to;
    if (!ci) return 'not_applicable';
    
    var threshold = gs.daysAgoStart(30);
    
    // Query for outstanding critical patches
    var gr = new GlideRecord('cmdb_ci_patch');
    gr.addQuery('cmdb_ci', ci);
    gr.addQuery('severity', 'critical');
    gr.addQuery('state', '!=', 'applied');
    gr.addQuery('release_date', '<=', threshold);
    gr.query();
    
    if (gr.getRowCount() > 0) {
        // Store details as supporting data
        indicator.supporting_data = 
            gr.getRowCount() + ' critical patches overdue';
        return 'fail';
    }
    
    return 'pass';
})(control, indicator);</code></pre>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="tab-panel" id="tab-ind-incident">
                            <div class="code-block">
                                <div class="code-header">
                                    <span class="code-lang">Scripted Indicator — Incident SLA Compliance</span>
                                    <button class="code-copy">Copy</button>
                                </div>
                                <div class="code-body">
<pre><code>// Check: Are P1 incidents resolved within SLA?
(function(control, indicator) {
    var ci = control.profile.applies_to;
    if (!ci) return 'not_applicable';
    
    var ninetyDaysAgo = gs.daysAgoStart(90);
    
    // Count P1 incidents that breached SLA
    var gr = new GlideRecord('incident');
    gr.addQuery('cmdb_ci', ci);
    gr.addQuery('priority', '1');
    gr.addQuery('opened_at', '>=', ninetyDaysAgo);
    gr.addQuery('made_sla', false);
    gr.query();
    
    var breachCount = gr.getRowCount();
    
    if (breachCount > 0) {
        indicator.supporting_data = 
            breachCount + ' P1 SLA breaches in 90 days';
        return 'fail';
    }
    
    return 'pass';
})(control, indicator);</code></pre>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="tab-panel" id="tab-ind-change">
                            <div class="code-block">
                                <div class="code-header">
                                    <span class="code-lang">Scripted Indicator — Unauthorized Changes</span>
                                    <button class="code-copy">Copy</button>
                                </div>
                                <div class="code-body">
<pre><code>// Check: Were all changes to this CI properly approved?
(function(control, indicator) {
    var ci = control.profile.applies_to;
    if (!ci) return 'not_applicable';
    
    var thirtyDaysAgo = gs.daysAgoStart(30);
    
    // Find changes without proper approval
    var gr = new GlideRecord('change_request');
    gr.addQuery('cmdb_ci', ci);
    gr.addQuery('sys_created_on', '>=', thirtyDaysAgo);
    gr.addQuery('approval', '!=', 'approved');
    gr.addQuery('state', 'closed');
    gr.query();
    
    if (gr.getRowCount() > 0) {
        indicator.supporting_data = 
            gr.getRowCount() + ' unapproved changes detected';
        return 'fail';
    }
    
    return 'pass';
})(control, indicator);</code></pre>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- Flow Designer -->
                <section class="content-section" id="flow-designer">
                    <h2>Flow Designer Patterns</h2>
                    <p>
                        <strong>Flow Designer</strong> is the preferred way to build automation in IRM (over legacy 
                        Workflows). Common patterns include:
                    </p>

                    <div class="accordion">
                        <div class="accordion-item open">
                            <button class="accordion-trigger">
                                <span class="accordion-trigger-text">Auto-Create Issue on Indicator Failure</span>
                                <span class="accordion-icon">▾</span>
                            </button>
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                <div class="accordion-content">
                                    <p><strong>Trigger:</strong> Record Updated on <code>sn_grc_indicator_result</code> where result = 'fail'</p>
                                    <p><strong>Actions:</strong></p>
                                    <p>
                                        1. Look up the related control and entity<br>
                                        2. Check if an open issue already exists for this control<br>
                                        3. If no existing issue → Create new <code>sn_grc_issue</code> record<br>
                                        4. Assign to control owner<br>
                                        5. Send notification to risk manager
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="accordion-item">
                            <button class="accordion-trigger">
                                <span class="accordion-trigger-text">Risk Appetite Breach Escalation</span>
                                <span class="accordion-icon">▾</span>
                            </button>
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                <div class="accordion-content">
                                    <p><strong>Trigger:</strong> Record Updated on <code>sn_risk_risk</code> where residual_risk changed</p>
                                    <p><strong>Actions:</strong></p>
                                    <p>
                                        1. Compare new residual risk score against risk appetite threshold<br>
                                        2. If over appetite → Move risk state to "Respond"<br>
                                        3. Create approval request for risk response<br>
                                        4. Notify risk committee members<br>
                                        5. Create calendar event for review meeting
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="accordion-item">
                            <button class="accordion-trigger">
                                <span class="accordion-trigger-text">Automated Evidence Request Workflow</span>
                                <span class="accordion-icon">▾</span>
                            </button>
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                <div class="accordion-content">
                                    <p><strong>Trigger:</strong> Record Created on audit test execution record</p>
                                    <p><strong>Actions:</strong></p>
                                    <p>
                                        1. Identify required evidence types from test template<br>
                                        2. Look up control owner for the in-scope control<br>
                                        3. Create evidence request record with due date<br>
                                        4. Send personalized email with specific evidence instructions<br>
                                        5. Schedule reminder at 75% of due date if not submitted<br>
                                        6. Escalate to manager if overdue
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- Business Rules -->
                <section class="content-section" id="business-rules">
                    <h2>Business Rules</h2>
                    <p>
                        Some common business rule patterns used in IRM customizations:
                    </p>

                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">
                            <span class="code-lang">Business Rule — Auto-Assign Risk Owner from Entity</span>
                            <button class="code-copy">Copy</button>
                        </div>
                        <div class="code-body">
<pre><code>// Table: sn_risk_risk
// When: Before Insert
// Condition: Risk owner is empty

(function executeRule(current, previous) {
    if (!current.risk_owner) {
        // Inherit owner from the entity
        var entity = new GlideRecord('sn_grc_profile');
        if (entity.get(current.profile)) {
            current.risk_owner = entity.owned_by;
            gs.info('Auto-assigned risk owner from entity: ' 
                    + entity.owned_by.getDisplayValue());
        }
    }
})(current, previous);</code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">
                            <span class="code-lang">Business Rule — Cascade Entity Deactivation</span>
                            <button class="code-copy">Copy</button>
                        </div>
                        <div class="code-body">
<pre><code>// Table: sn_grc_profile
// When: After Update
// Condition: active changes to false

(function executeRule(current, previous) {
    // When an entity is deactivated, close all
    // associated controls and risks
    
    // Close controls
    var ctrl = new GlideRecord('sn_compliance_control');
    ctrl.addQuery('profile', current.sys_id);
    ctrl.addActiveQuery();
    ctrl.query();
    while (ctrl.next()) {
        ctrl.state = 'not_applicable';
        ctrl.active = false;
        ctrl.update();
    }
    
    // Retire risks
    var risk = new GlideRecord('sn_risk_risk');
    risk.addQuery('profile', current.sys_id);
    risk.addQuery('state', '!=', 'retired');
    risk.query();
    while (risk.next()) {
        risk.state = 'retired';
        risk.update();
    }
    
    gs.info('Cascaded deactivation for entity: ' 
            + current.name);
})(current, previous);</code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- Best Practices -->
                <section class="content-section" id="best-practices">
                    <h2>Best Practices</h2>

                    <div class="info-card info-card--tip">
                        <div class="info-card-title">1. Use the Entity Framework — Don't Hardcode</div>
                        <p>
                            Always leverage Entity Types and their dynamic filters to associate risks and 
                            controls with assets. Never hardcode entity-to-CI mappings. When a new CI is 
                            added to the CMDB that matches an Entity Type filter, IRM should automatically 
                            create the corresponding entity and scope controls to it.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="info-card info-card--tip">
                        <div class="info-card-title">2. Align with CSDM</div>
                        <p>
                            When modeling your entities, align them with the Common Service Data Model (CSDM). 
                            This ensures risk data remains consistent with your service architecture and enables 
                            service-level risk reporting.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="info-card info-card--tip">
                        <div class="info-card-title">3. Prefer Configuration Over Customization</div>
                        <p>
                            IRM provides extensive configuration options (RAM, Entity Types, Content References, 
                            Indicator Templates). Exhaust these before writing custom scripts. Custom code 
                            increases upgrade complexity and can break platform automation that relies on the 
                            standard schema.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="info-card info-card--tip">
                        <div class="info-card-title">4. Use Scoped APIs</div>
                        <p>
                            Always use the <code>sn_grc</code> and <code>sn_compliance</code> scoped APIs when 
                            available. These enforce data integrity constraints and business logic that raw 
                            GlideRecord operations might bypass.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="info-card info-card--tip">
                        <div class="info-card-title">5. Test in Sub-Production</div>
                        <p>
                            IRM configurations can have cascading effects (e.g., changing an Entity Type filter 
                            can generate or remove hundreds of controls). Always test configuration changes in 
                            a sub-production instance first.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- Common Pitfalls -->
                <section class="content-section" id="common-pitfalls">
                    <h2>Common Pitfalls</h2>

                    <div class="info-card info-card--warning">
                        <div class="info-card-title">⚠ Writing Directly to M2M Tables</div>
                        <p>
                            Inserting or deleting records directly in M2M join tables (e.g., 
                            <code>sn_grc_m2m_cont_ref_control</code>) can corrupt data relationships. 
                            Use the UI or scoped APIs to manage these relationships.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="info-card info-card--warning">
                        <div class="info-card-title">⚠ Ignoring Application Scope</div>
                        <p>
                            IRM tables are scoped to <code>sn_grc</code>, <code>sn_compliance</code>, etc. 
                            If your custom scripts or integrations don't run in the correct scope, they may 
                            fail with "access denied" errors or silently skip records they can't see.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="info-card info-card--warning">
                        <div class="info-card-title">⚠ Over-Customizing Control Generation</div>
                        <p>
                            The Content Reference mechanism automatically generates controls based on Entity 
                            Type and Control Objective combinations. Custom scripts that also generate controls 
                            can lead to duplicates and data quality issues. Understand the OOB generation 
                            logic before adding custom creation logic.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="info-card info-card--warning">
                        <div class="info-card-title">⚠ Not Handling "Not Applicable" in Indicators</div>
                        <p>
                            Always handle the case where an indicator can't determine pass/fail (e.g., 
                            the entity has no associated CI). Returning <code>'not_applicable'</code> is 
                            better than returning <code>'fail'</code> — false positives erode trust in 
                            your compliance data.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>

